# Issue 3: Windows Agent Not Connecting

## Problem

After installing the Windows Agent, the endpoint did not immediately appear in the Wazuh Dashboard.

---

## Cause

Although the Wazuh Agent had been installed successfully, its Windows service was not running.

---

## Resolution

I first verified whether the service existed.

```powershell
Get-Service WazuhSvc
```

Then I started the service manually.

```cmd
NET START WazuhSvc
```

Within a few moments, the Windows endpoint appeared in the dashboard with an **Active** status.

---

# Issue 4: Incorrect Service Name

## Problem

While attempting to start the Windows Agent, I initially executed:

```powershell
Start-Service Wazuh-Svc
```

PowerShell returned an error stating that the service could not be found.

---

## Cause

I used an incorrect service name.

---

## Resolution

The correct Windows service name is:

```cmd
NET START WazuhSvc
```

After using the correct command, the service started successfully.

