# Lessons Learned

Building this SIEM lab provided several practical lessons beyond simply following the installation documentation.

- Ubuntu's automatic updates can interrupt long-running package installations.
- Verifying every service after installation helps identify incomplete deployments.
- Bridged networking is more suitable than NAT when virtual machines need to communicate directly with physical hosts.
- DHCP-assigned IP addresses may change after a reboot, which can cause agents to disconnect if they rely on a fixed manager address.
- Reviewing logs and checking service status should always be the first step before considering a complete reinstallation.

Most of the issues I encountered were caused by configuration rather than software failures. Working through each problem individually helped me better understand how the different Wazuh components interact and communicate within a SIEM environment.
